1
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:34,980
Why?

2
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,240
Afraid to search?

3
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:38,410
Then let him do it for you.

4
00:00:48,510 --> 00:00:50,670
It's time for you to taste it.

5
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:53,830
This...

6
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:54,580
This is...

7
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:00,330
Guard the door.

8
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:02,770
Understood.

9
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:16,300
[Eclipse in the Lost City; Episode 5]

10
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,330
Who ordered you to do this?

11
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:21,390
Speak!

12
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:21,930
No.

13
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,240
I didn't do it.

14
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:26,030
Do you think I'd believe that?

15
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:28,700
You established yourself in Ningcheng
with those goods, didn't you?

16
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,360
Regarding my father's death,

17
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:31,870
whoever benefits the most

18
00:01:31,870 --> 00:01:32,990
is the killer.

19
00:01:33,490 --> 00:01:34,810
I only took the goods.

20
00:01:34,830 --> 00:01:35,990
But I didn't kill

21
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:37,130
Qinglong.

22
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:38,350
Stop making excuses.

23
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,620
The old chief trusted you so much.

24
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:42,570
Back then,

25
00:01:42,590 --> 00:01:44,789
he saved your life with a silver needle.

26
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,690
But you bite the hand that feeds you.

27
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,620
You've been by the old chief's side
for so many years.

28
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:52,200
I'm afraid you’ve had ulterior motives
all along.

29
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,039
How dare you

30
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:54,190
talk nonsense!

31
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:56,030
I didn't kill the old chief.

32
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:57,670
It's come to this,

33
00:01:58,380 --> 00:01:59,979
and you still won't confess?

34
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:04,820
Lu Ye.

35
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:06,540
You will regret this.

36
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,120
Do you really think you can trap me?

37
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:11,420
I've already prepared a backup plan.

38
00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:12,910
A backup plan?

39
00:02:19,410 --> 00:02:20,730
All your men are here.

40
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,920
Which one are you talking about?

41
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:32,000
Young Master.

42
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,570
I really shouldn't have
embezzled those goods.

43
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:34,850
Please forgive me.

44
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:36,200
Give me one more chance.

45
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:37,450
Alright.

46
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:40,500
Then let's follow the rules of
the Qingtian Gang.

47
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:41,300
Three stabs.

48
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:43,140
If you survive them,

49
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:44,579
I'll spare your life.

50
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:45,310
No.

51
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:46,110
No.

52
00:02:53,890 --> 00:02:56,650
The first stab is for your disloyalty.

53
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:58,730
Young Master, I know I was wrong.

54
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:02,510
The second stab is for your cruelty.

55
00:03:02,650 --> 00:03:04,170
I won't do it again.

56
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:07,150
The third stab

57
00:03:07,510 --> 00:03:08,770
is for your injustice.

58
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,380
Let the blood flow.

59
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,220
Once the filth in your bones is drained,

60
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:20,130
consider it your atonement.

61
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:26,750
As long as you can step out of this door,

62
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:30,060
you and the Qingtian Gang are even.

63
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:08,080
Just one step away.

64
00:04:08,470 --> 00:04:09,550
What a pity.

65
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,260
Seems like you're out of luck.

66
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:16,079
Young Master,

67
00:04:16,579 --> 00:04:17,860
spare my life.

68
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:22,560
The old chief wouldn't want to see you

69
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:24,560
become like this.

70
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:34,909
You're right.

71
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:38,330
He really didn't want me
to get blood on my hands.

72
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,720
Too bad.

73
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:45,590
People change.

74
00:04:59,230 --> 00:05:00,030
Aunt Que.

75
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,100
I'm sorry.

76
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:04,380
I had to confirm who was involved.

77
00:05:05,010 --> 00:05:06,540
It was a misunderstanding.

78
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:08,200
Sorry for startling you.

79
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:12,550
Young Master.

80
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,560
This...

81
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:14,810
Please accept it.

82
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:16,950
I...

83
00:05:17,950 --> 00:05:19,930
You've worked hard all these years.

84
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:22,460
Consider it a thank you
on behalf of my father.

85
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,280
Young Master,

86
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:30,990
my condolences.

87
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:52,400
You did a good job today.

88
00:05:53,050 --> 00:05:54,550
You flatter me, Young Master.

89
00:05:54,550 --> 00:05:56,250
They don't know you've lost your memory.

90
00:05:56,250 --> 00:05:57,130
Originally,

91
00:05:57,330 --> 00:05:58,800
I just wanted to use your title as sheriff

92
00:05:58,800 --> 00:05:59,600
to bluff them.

93
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:01,250
I was even afraid you'd get stage fright.

94
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:04,090
I didn't expect you to perform so well.

95
00:06:05,310 --> 00:06:06,940
It's all thanks to your teaching,
Young Master.

96
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:07,740
Wrong.

97
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:08,980
It wasn't me.

98
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,810
You deserve the credit.

99
00:06:11,910 --> 00:06:14,550
Tell me, is your acting just that good,

100
00:06:16,180 --> 00:06:17,140
or

101
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,980
have you recovered your memory?

102
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:23,050
No.

103
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:25,840
I still can't remember anything.

104
00:06:32,409 --> 00:06:33,210
Is that so?

105
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:36,080
Then why do you remember this?

106
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:41,909
Oh no.

107
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,659
Guard the door.

108
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:48,720
Give me an explanation.

109
00:06:49,820 --> 00:06:50,620
Young Master,

110
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:52,720
I...

111
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:55,470
I didn't even notice your action
at the time.

112
00:06:56,340 --> 00:06:58,390
I just guessed
that Qinglong would run away,

113
00:06:58,390 --> 00:06:59,650
so I stopped him first.

114
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:02,960
Young Master,

115
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:04,550
did I do something wrong?

116
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:10,350
I'm sorry.

117
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:12,790
It's my fault for acting on my own.

118
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:14,660
Forget it.

119
00:07:15,490 --> 00:07:16,620
I was overthinking.

120
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:18,290
Let's drink.

121
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:21,030
Young Master,

122
00:07:21,030 --> 00:07:21,710
please.

123
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:23,500
To the Qingtian Gang.

124
00:07:23,690 --> 00:07:24,890
To the Qingtian Gang.

125
00:07:41,570 --> 00:07:42,370
Who is it?

126
00:07:43,770 --> 00:07:45,420
It's you again, Shen Tianbai.

127
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,100
Are you crazy?

128
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,380
You skipped class.

129
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,310
Go back to class.

130
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,060
What’s it to you
whether I go to class or not?

131
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:54,790
Who are you to tell me what to do?

132
00:07:55,409 --> 00:07:56,909
You think I want to babysit you?

133
00:07:56,909 --> 00:07:59,580
But the school said
your dad funds my scholarship.

134
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:01,200
He only asked me to do one thing.

135
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,930
And that's to keep an eye on you.

136
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:07,800
Can't you just make something up?

137
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:09,720
The old man believes whatever you say
anyway.

138
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:11,080
Why should I lie for you?

139
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,100
Go call for help.

140
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,080
Without me,

141
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:21,040
how will you claim credit from my father?

142
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,530
Trying to call for help?

143
00:08:25,620 --> 00:08:27,030
It's the same trick every time.

144
00:08:27,030 --> 00:08:27,980
I've seen it twice.

145
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,440
Even a fool could guess it.

146
00:08:30,330 --> 00:08:30,930
You...

147
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:32,980
Let's go.

148
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:35,440
You can still make it
to the afternoon class.

149
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,380
Let me go.

150
00:08:37,409 --> 00:08:39,380
Since when do you get to tell me
what to do?

151
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,179
Let me go.

152
00:08:49,980 --> 00:08:50,950
Are you awake?

153
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:53,240
How could Mr. Lu have a son like you?

154
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:55,140
What else can you do
besides spending money?

155
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:57,070
Then why don't you just go be his son?

156
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:59,000
He only likes sons like you anyway.

157
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:03,880
What's wrong?

158
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:11,320
We're even.

159
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:13,780
Childish.

160
00:09:13,850 --> 00:09:14,770
Yes, yes.

161
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,780
You are the most mature.

162
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:16,580
Prude.

163
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:18,770
Your father is right.

164
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:21,320
You are just a useless piece of trash.

165
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,440
Right.

166
00:09:24,590 --> 00:09:26,040
He looks down on me anyway.

167
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,640
Sometimes I really envy you.

168
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,500
No parents, no one to control you.

169
00:09:59,000 --> 00:09:59,920
You deserve it.

170
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,600
Likewise.

171
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:05,300
Alright.

172
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:07,860
Now we don't have to go to class.

173
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:09,430
In your dreams.

174
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:14,580
There's another class in the afternoon.

175
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:15,380
We can make it.

176
00:10:17,390 --> 00:10:19,190
You want to go to class like this?

177
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:20,280
I can say

178
00:10:21,550 --> 00:10:22,880
we went to do a good deed.

179
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:26,820
When did you learn to lie?

180
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,280
I learned it from you.

181
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:39,650
The mole is caught.

182
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:40,990
Tonight,

183
00:10:42,030 --> 00:10:43,960
we can all get a good night's sleep.

184
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:48,460
Drink.

185
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:54,500
You think this can trap me?
